+// CHANCE. process() takes an optional per-step chance, a percentage clamped
+// to 0..100; the six-argument form is chance 100 and behaves exactly as it
+// did before chance existed. The chance is applied once, when the playhead
+// LANDS on a step (a clock edge or a reset), and only if that step is a hit:
+// a rest rolls nothing, chance 100 plays the hit and rolls nothing, chance 0
+// silences it and rolls nothing, anything between makes exactly one
+// rng.percent() call and plays the hit when the result is below the chance.
+// A step that lost its roll is a rest for the whole stay (no TRIG, GATE low
+// on every sample until the playhead moves); idle samples never re-roll, and
+// nothing else consumes the generator. The pattern table is never touched:
+// the loss is held in Sequencer::muted. load() does not roll, so step 1's
+// GATE after load follows the pattern. The generator is Rng, a xorshift32 the
+// caller may seed for a reproducible run.
+//
